{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1791321000000-reviewer-d14-source-gate.opus.stdout.log; tail -100 collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.findings.md; git status --short; git diff --stat'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-06 22:44:20 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-07 05:44:20 +07\n\n# Gate review: M-next D14 (source/exit half with progress journal)\n\n**Verdict: NOT READY**\n\nThe new freeze/rehydrate seam does its job. It has its own tag and version 1 and reuses the handoff codec. It checks addresses, the header, descriptors, the snapshot against the body and the recovery state before anything is attached. It proves byte identity by re-preparing and re-encoding, with zero IO calls, and a recovered record cannot abort (`export.cljc:313-485`, `:527`). The exit order matches the ruling (`driver.cljc:1243-1270`). Acknowledgments are matched to the exact request: the report id carries `[o1 l address]` and the release id carries the lease (`driver.cljc:1148-1150`, `:1327-1331`, `:2292-2313`).\n\nFour defects block landing: two high-severity, two medium.\n\n## Blocking findings\n\n**1. (High) A non-admitted report answer wedges the exit forever while the lease keeps being renewed.**\n- `step-exit-body` turns any non-admitted report answer into a permanent `:report-refused` (`driver.cljc:1263-1265`). There is no resend, no run end and no release.\n- `step-active-held` still renews on every step before entering the exit body (`driver.cljc:1982-1989`). The holder therefore keeps the occurrence alive indefinitely, and it never closes or becomes regrantable.\n- `completion/report!` documents the authority's own `:suspended` and `:closed` answers. `:suspended` is transient, so it should lead to a resend. The terminal refusals (`:ended-lease`, `:quarantined`, `:report-conflict`, `:counter-regression`) should run the r3 1.6 run-end: one diagnostic plus cleanup release.\n- No test drives a refused or suspended report.\n\n**2. (High) Abort is not journaled, so a reopen brings back an aborted first export and offers its stale snapshot.**\n- `abort*` (`driver.cljc:2498-2556`) changes only the in-memory state. The journal still holds the `:first` mint and fence.\n- After a crash, `reopen` sends that journal through `reopen-source` (`driver.cljc:2415-2416`, `:2201-2227`). It rebuilds the fenced snapshot and `step-exporting` sends the offer.\n- But the aborted machine had already returned to local, uncustodied execution and may have performed IO after the snapshot. If the offer is admitted and granted, the stale checkpoint runs again: double execution and duplicated effects.\n- Abort needs a durable terminal record (for example `{:yin.k/journal :yin.k/aborted :yin.k/occurrence O}`), written before local execution is handed back. The fold and reopen must then treat it as closing the export.\n- No test reopens after an abort.\n\n**3. (Medium) A holder that crashes during exit preparation, before the fence, stays stalled forever and never releases or re-proposes.**\n- The first `reopen` branch (`driver.cljc:2405-2408`) stalls on any minted-but-unfenced occurrence, including a successor or result minted after a journaled grant.\n- `:stalled` refuses all progress, and reopening again gives the same answer. The origin lease is never released, and this driver never re-enters candidacy.\n- That contradicts:\n  - the ruling §1: \"a restarted holder releases and re-enters candidacy\";\n  - brief item 9;\n  - the new UCF text: \"they reconcile, release and re-enter candidacy\".\n- Releasing the origin lease and re-proposing over the origin checkpoint is not one of the ruling's forbidden moves (inventing waits, reminting, blind re-serving, or using the original machine). Only a `:first` source should stay non-runnable here; when a grant exists, this case belongs in `reopen-holder`.\n- `exit-journal-cuts-never-restore-execution-test` (`driver_test.cljc:2644-2679`) only asserts \"not running\" plus one step. It passes on this permanent stall and never checks that the release eventually happens.\n\n**4. (Medium) The abort tenure check ignores dao.lease's max cap and its bound latches.**\n- `abort*` computes the bound as `(or last-renewal-at granted-at) + duration` (`driver.cljc:2526-2531`).\n- dao.lease's `at-bound?` also enforces `:dao.lease/max` from `granted-at`, plus the sticky `:bound-reached?` and `:undersized?` latches (`dao/lease.cljc:1818-1832`).\n- UCF grants do carry `:dao.lease/max` (`ledger.cljc:78`, `authority/grant.cljc:153`). A holder past its cap but inside its renewal window can therefore abort back into execution. The ledger's `:live` check only closes that window once the judge's lapse has been folded.\n- The fix: decide tenure with `lease/holding?` and derive `:bound` from the same rule.\n\n## Non-blocking findings\n\n5. **(Low/Plausible) Restart cleanup can drop the exit cell.** In `step-exiting` (`driver.cljc:1297-1308`), a restarted exit clears `:exit` once release carriage is acknowledged and the ledger fold, read in the same step, does not yet show the report. If carriage acknowledgment can arrive before the earlier report is visible in the ledger, the closed occurrence's successor is never offered (the driver then answers `:not-holder` in proposing). Please confirm that the front guarantees ledger visibility before carriage replies, or keep the exit cell until the fold shows the lease ended.\n\n6. **(Low) The driver hard-codes the journal's cursor shape.** `journal-records` checks `:dao.stream.memory-log/identity` and `/position` keys (`driver.cljc:451-458`). That is backend knowledge inside the driver. It is consistent with journal.cljc's stated visible log, but brittle. Separately, malformed or unavailable history throws `ex-info` (with an `:assembly` hint) rather than returning a data refusal. That fails closed, which is acceptable, but the hint is misleading.\n\n7. **(Low/Needs confirmation) Version-1 published bytes may have changed.** `handoff.cljc:793` now runs the module-store fixed-point for `(:v1 @found)` too, not only for recovery. If a v1 body previously omitted transitive module stores, its published v1 bytes change. The ruling says \"Semantic handoff versions 0/1 and their bytes remain unchanged\", and the findings only mention leaving v0 unchanged. This needs a statement that `canonical-order` already covered these stores, or an architect note that this is a correction rather than a format change.\n\n8. **(Low) Small cleanups.**\n   - A freshly minted proposal intent is journaled twice before its first send (`driver.cljc:1407-1418`).\n   - `export-fence-step`'s eager `mapv` still stores the body after the recovery store has failed (`driver.cljc:866-881`). The fence stays correctly gated either way.\n\n9. **(Low) Seam test coverage.** `recovery-preserves-aliases-distinct-cells-and-authentic-closures-test` proves an authentic, receiver-owned closure held in the store. It does not test a closure captured in the blocked frame's environment registers, which is the ruling's \"closure inside waits\" case. Adding a `let1 'f (lam …)` / block / `(app (v 'f))` row would close that.\n\n## Regression check against D13/D11/D12\n\nI found no regression to the landed D13 candidate path: admitted-variant check, grant durable before lower, bound-before-apply renewal, run-end single diagnostic. Stall refusal covers `step`, `hand-off`, `abort` and `enroll`. Enrollment follows C12: every enroll call is preceded by a projection reread, and unavailable evidence waits.\n\nThe engineer's JVM 3556/235377 green result was not re-run, as instructed. Nothing was edited and no suite was run.\n  ordering, the report-answer run-end, the abort terminal record, the\n  tenure recheck and the deferred release.\n- this report.\n\n## Whole-task contract audit (condensed; final state)\n\n| Contract | Final behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. Export / fork / prepare | Landed enter/prepare/encode retained, alias-aware serving included. Nil arbitration is the version-0 fork: no occurrence, no offer, no journal bracket, the bytes answered. |\n| 2. Mint once before prepare | Occurrence and header journaled before prepare; serving and each store put write-ahead-bracketed; the recovery object precedes the body and a refused store stops before the body is attempted; both durable before the `fenced` record. |\n| 3. Brackets / stable proposals | Intent before every send, attempt after, authenticated acknowledgment when an answer stands; a resent proposal keeps its id, a refusal mints fresh; the first proposal send carries exactly one intent and one attempt. |\n| 4. Abort / attempts | Journaled attempts only; unmatched intents retain unknown delivery; the terminal `:yin.k/aborted` record is durable before hand-back and closes the export at reopen (both roles pinned); a holder rechecks `lease/holding?` — cap and latches — after the record, and a bound crossed under it ends the run with the release deferred to the next step; recovered records refuse `:restarted`; a holder past its bound never restores its old machine. |\n| 5. Exit / cuts / halt | Persist recovery and body, fence, offer, report the exact body, release the matching origin lease, observe the closure and successor edge, retry the same offer until admitted; `:awaiting-completion` never blocks reporting; `:suspended` resends the identical report; terminal refusals run the 1.6 run-end; a halt reports its result body with a terminal edge and no successor offer. |\n| 6. Tenure through exit | Renewal before half the duration and the recheck before every exit action; all IO stops at the bound; the settled exit (release carried) watches the ledger without spending tenure. |\n| 7. Reopen | Complete fenced snapshots rebuilt from canonical recovery bytes in the store — never a supplied machine; same occurrence, waits, retained ids, descriptors and byte identity; incomplete preparations stay non-runnable; a minted-but-unfenced exit releases and re-enters candidacy while only a `:first` source stalls; an aborted export is closed at reopen. |\n| 8. Uncertain append | Step, abort, enroll and hand-off refuse progression while stalled; reads distinguish authenticated end-of-history from transport failure, gaps and malformed frames; only reopen reconciles. |\n| 9. Holder recovery | A journaled grant never restores execution: the pending release is sent and candidacy re-entered; newer grants outrank old exits; old release acknowledgments cannot discharge another lease; the admitted-variant proof retained. |\n| 10. C12 enrollment | Identity discipline: the derived target identity is journaled with the intent, an uncertain answer is reconciled by rereading the projection, one more attempt only when absent; progress survives reopen. |\n| 11. Run end / residual 2 | `:stale`, `:intent-conflict`, `:input-conflict`, divergence, the bound — and now the report refusals and the abort's crossed bound — gate `:ended`, stop all program IO, append one diagnostic, release as cleanup; a release never closes an occurrence without accepted completion evidence; after divergence the released occurrence is regrantable; after `:intent-conflict` it stays quarantined and ungrantable. |\n\n## Exact tests and checks\n\n| Gate | Outcome | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver-test` | 77 tests, 1171 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors | observed in-session |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.holder.export-test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v1-test` | 70 tests, 714 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors | observed in-session |\n| all four focused suites in one run | 147 tests, 1885 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors | `build/d14-gatefix/focused-four.log` |\n| full JVM fast lane (`clojure -M:test -e :slow` over the standing `build/yin-repl-node` and ANTLR artifacts; `bb` is not on this session's PATH) | **3568 tests, 235534 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors; exit 0** | `build/d14-gatefix/full-fast-lane.log` |\n| kondo (`clojure -M:kondo --lint`) on the five files | **blocked this session** — the alias command needs an approval this delegated session cannot grant, and the ProcessBuilder spawn route (the prior round's workaround) is filtered at the JVM level here: `ClassNotFoundException: java.util.ProcessBuilder` from inside an allowlisted `clojure -M -e` | noted per the brief |\n| cljstyle | **blocked** — no binary on PATH and both indirect routes hit the same walls as kondo | noted per the brief |\n| `git diff --check` | clean, exit 0 | observed in-session |\n| git writes | none | `git status` unchanged in shape all session |\n\nkondo/cljstyle caveat, precisely: the prior round's green lint verdicts\n(`0 errors, 0 warnings`, `/private/tmp/d14-final-kondo6.log`; `5 files\nchecked`, `/private/tmp/d14-final-style4.log`) cover the files as they\nstood before this session's hunks. This session's edits were formatted\nby hand to each file's existing conventions (alignment, docstring\nstyle, the `--` dash convention), `git diff --check` is clean, and the\nJVM compiler accepted every hunk, but the tools' own verdicts on the\nfinal text have not been obtained.\n\n## Red and green evidence\n\nThe partial round handed off exactly two red rows — the session's first\nact was running the driver suite before any edit (76 tests, 1157\nassertions, 4 failures, 0 errors; verbatim block preserved at\n`build/d14-gatefix/red-at-handoff.log`):\n\n| Red row at hand-off | Red outcome | Green evidence after the fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `failed-recovery-store-does-not-attempt-the-body-store-test` | `@calls` 2 ≠ 1 — both store puts attempted | driver suite 77/1171, 0 failures |\n| `abort-rechecks-tenure-after-its-durable-terminal-record-test` | abort answered `:yin.k/ok`, `:running`, machine `:running` instead of `:yin.k/ended`, `:releasing`, gate `:ended` | same run |\n\nRows added this session, stated honestly:\n\n- The deferred-release completion leg on the recheck row was written\n  after the fix, not before; against the pre-fix code it cannot pass\n  (the pre-fix abort answers `:running`, so driving to `:failed` from\n  it cannot succeed), so the row is red-by-construction on the\n  inherited defect, but no separate red run of it was captured.\n- `aborted-hand-off-reopen-closes-the-export-and-reenters-candidacy-test`\n  pinned already-correct fold behavior and was green on arrival. Its\n  first draft failed for a wrong reason — the assertion counted the\n  source's own first-export offer, which legitimately stands in the\n  inbound ring — and the assertion was corrected to name the aborted\n  successor's occurrence; no production code changed for it.\n\nInherited red/green cycles (the seam and journal rebuild rounds, by the\nprior engineers; logs still on disk under `/private/tmp/`): recovery\nAPIs 16/86/6/0 → seam green; validation 17/110/3/0 → green;\nalias/cell bytes 18/124/5/2 → green; storage brackets 55/524/7/0 →\n56/531 green; grant durability 64/1010/1/0 → green; receiver\ncontamination 21/140/4/0 → green; FFI route 24/166/3/0 → green;\nlegacy dependencies 24/168/4/0 → green; snapshot binding 24/174/2/0 →\ngreen; stalled hand-off 1/3/1/0 → green; delayed report carriage\n1/9/3/0 → 65/1020 green; renewal brackets 2/29/5/0 → 66/1026 green.\nThe inherited baseline was 48 driver tests / 490 assertions / 24\nfailures / 1 error (`/private/tmp/d14-baseline.log`). This session's\nstarting point was the partial round's 76/1157/4/0.\n\n## Remaining concerns / incomplete work\n\n- The gate log was unreadable from this session (above); the six items\n  were addressed from the dispatch's distillation. A reviewer with the\n  gate's text should confirm the mapping, especially the exact\n  semantics the gate attached to \"small cleanups\".\n- kondo and cljstyle verdicts on the final text were not obtained\n  (approval-blocked); see the caveat above.\n- Dedicated Node and Dart lanes were not run this session (JVM during\n  iteration, per the acceptance criteria); the standing artifacts the\n  fast lane depends on (`target/yin-repl.js`, `build/antlr`) are the\n  prior round's.\n- The inherited conservative interpretations stand unchanged: a\n  restarted holder does not resend an uncommitted report under saved\n  tenure (it carries cleanup release and reconciles; a late original\n  carriage still completes its exit), and incomplete snapshots or\n  unavailable history fail closed.\n- Architect/reviewer validation of the whole round is still owed; this\n  is implementation evidence, not a sign-off.\n M docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc\n?? collab/1791194000000-architect-m-next-d-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1791231000000-architect-d9-header-ruling.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1791240000000-architect-d10-lower-inputs-ruling.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.findings.md\n?? collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791320000000-architect-d14-seam-ruling-astra.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/d14-fulltest.log\n .../design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md |   54 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc                   |  208 ++-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc             | 1976 ++++++++++++++++++--\n src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc             |  218 ++-\n test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc            | 1496 ++++++++++++++-\n test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc            |  362 ++++\n 6 files changed, 4046 insertions(+), 268 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
